 "text": "Nintendo is 137 years old, and it started with playing cards. Kyoto, Japan. Fusajiro Yamauchi opens a small shop making Japanese playing cards. Decades later, a new boss, Hiroshi Yamauchi, wants more than cards. Nintendo tries a taxi company. Instant rice. None of it lasts. By the mid-1960s, Nintendo is close to going broke. Then the boss visits a card factory and spots a young engineer, Gunpei Yokoi, playing with an arm he built for fun. He tells him, turn it into a toy. The ultra-hand sells over a million. And that engineer? He later led the team behind the Game Boy, a card shop that became a gaming giant. Every legend has a beginning.",
